{"id":102252755886483,"type":"song","name":"Lotus Flower","artist":"Radiohead","year":2011,"weight":12,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/cover/a8ce38894d6a4a08e8559bb3b8c22fc3/250x250-000000-80-0-0.jpg","album":"The King Of Limbs","yt":"cfOa1a8hYP8"},"artist_ref":{"id":82720776946884,"name":"Radiohead","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/RadioheadO2211125_composite.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[],"lists":[{"id":99660559267786,"name":"Triple J Hottest 100 · 2011","src":"singles","grp":"triple_j_hottest_100","list_year":2011,"rank":61,"year":2011,"note":"United Kingdom","total":100,"scaruffi":null}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"Released as the sole official single from \"The King of Limbs\" album, this song represented the band's exploration into a studio-conceived sound characterized by loops, samples, and rhythm-heavy arrangements. \"They called it The King of Limbs and this was the first and only official single from the record. It's called Lotus Flower.\"","year":2011,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Radiohead - A History: Part 3","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vt6DVj7S6nk"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This song from the 2011 album \"King of Limbs\" is mentioned in conjunction with the discovery of an ant species named after Radiohead. It serves as a musical reference point connecting the band to the scientific tribute. \"And with Lotus Flower from their 2011 King of Lims, and they've got their own ant on the floor of the Venezuelan jungle.\"","year":2011,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"RocknRoll Scientific Nomenclature","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VMPLplhDk8I"}]}],"book_tracks":[],"others":[{"id":279914671926127,"type":"album","name":"OK Computer","year":1997,"weight":167},{"id":189423945548313,"type":"album","name":"Kid A","year":2000,"weight":124},{"id":9259407658